sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Sh as Shell
    participant K as Kernel
    participant Ch as Child process
    participant Bin as Program image
    Sh->>K: fork()
    K->>Ch: duplicate the address space, copy-on-write
    K-->>Sh: child PID
    K-->>Ch: returns 0
    Note over K,Ch: one call, two returns — that is how the parent tells them apart
    Ch->>K: execve(program)
    K->>Bin: load the ELF, map text, data, heap, stack
    K->>Ch: replace the image, keep the PID
    Note over Ch: fork makes a process, exec makes it a different program
    Ch->>K: exit(status)
    K-->>Sh: SIGCHLD
    Sh->>K: wait() collects the status
    Note over K,Sh: a child nobody waits for stays a zombie in the table
